erated":false,"label":"list_item","marker":"·","orig":"· Step 2: We now want to extend the non-degeneracy property of the gradient of u to the functions u j on their level sets u -1 j (0) . We notice that by uniform convergence and by the previous step, for every ε > 0 there exist t 0 > 0 and j 0 such that","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/2"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":312.7475825,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":79.19958200000013,"r":516.0200271633063,"t":351.7329341},"charspan":[0,252],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/15","text":"Step 2: We now want to extend the non-degeneracy property of the gradient of u to the functions u j on their level sets u -1 j (0) . We notice that by uniform convergence and by the previous step, for every ε > 0 there exist t 0 > 0 and j 0 such that"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"∀ j ≥ j 0 , u -1 j (0) ⊂ u -1 (( -t 0 , t 0 )) ⊂ ( u -1 (0)) ε . (A.2)","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":286.7073425000001,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":180.2395820000001,"r":517.3353742311081,"t":302.4774525},"charspan":[0,70],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/16","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"On the other hand, ∇ u is uniformly continuous in Ω so there exists α 0 > 0 such that","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":263.7873925000001,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":79.19984200000005,"r":482.7682346523511,"t":275.6527341000001},"charspan":[0,85],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/17","text":"On the other hand, ∇ u is uniformly continuous in Ω so there exists α 0 > 0 such that"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"∀ ( x, z ) ∈ Ω s.t. | z -x | ≤ α 0 , |∇ u ( z ) -∇ u ( x ) | ≤ k 4 .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":228.13272500000005,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":165.59992200000005,"r":429.74159069999996,"t":253.92193500000008},"charspan":[0,68],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/18","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"In particular,","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":208.692495,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":79.19977,"r":141.95732847974006,"t":219.61250410000002},"charspan":[0,14],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/19","text":"In particular,"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"∀ x ∈ ( u -1 (0)) α 0 , |∇ u ( x ) | ≥ k 2 .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":183.13272500000005,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":215.51977,"r":379.8219806999999,"t":208.9219250000001},"charspan":[0,44],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/20","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Also, ∇ u j uniformly converge to ∇ u , so for j large enough","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":167.1874325,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":78.84015999999997,"r":357.36587432357715,"t":179.05277410000008},"charspan":[0,61],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/21","text":"Also, ∇ u j uniformly converge to ∇ u , so for j large enough"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"formula","orig":"|∇ u j ( x ) -∇ u ( x ) | ≤ k 8 ∀ x ∈ Ω .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":130.572725,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":215.03974999999994,"r":380.1815806999999,"t":156.361805},"charspan":[0,41],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/22","text":""},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"From the previous estimates, we get |∇ u j | ( x ) > 0 for every x ∈ u -1 j (0) and j large enough, which implies that the sets u -1 j (0) are C 1 ,s hypersurfaces.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":90.86756249999996,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":78.83987999999994,"r":517.431576965764,"t":122.23769249999998},"charspan":[0,164],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/23","text":"From the previous estimates, we get |∇ u j | ( x ) > 0 for every x ∈ u -1 j (0) and j large enough, which implies that the sets u -1 j (0) are C 1 ,s hypersurfaces."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","labe